  "title": "Waltz time and 6/8",
  "summary": "Not everything counts in four.",
  "minutes": 6,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "3/4",
      "body": "In **3/4** there are three quarter-note beats in a bar: ONE two three, ONE two three. It is waltz time.\n\n**Why it matters:** Waltzes, many folk songs and some ballads (like Norwegian Wood) are in 3/4. Counting four to them feels wrong at once.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        60
      ],
      "labels": {
        "60": "ONE 2 3"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "6/8",
      "body": "In **6/8** there are six eighth-note beats in a bar, felt as two groups of three: ONE two three FOUR five six.\n\n**Why it matters:** It has a rolling, lilting feel heard in slow soul ballads and Irish jigs. House of the Rising Sun is in 6/8.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        60
      ],
      "labels": {
        "60": "ONE 2 3 FOUR 5 6"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "show",
      "title": "Three or six",
      "body": "Count \"ONE two three\" for 3/4, and \"ONE two three FOUR five six\" for 6/8.",
      "highlightMidi": [
        60
      ],
      "labels": {
        "60": "3/4 or 6/8"
      }
    },
